<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfonso VIII</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1155–<a href="/years/1214">1214</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfonso VIII was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> from 1158 to 1214. After being defeated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-alarcos">Alarcos</a> in 1195, he led a coalition of Christian kingdoms to a decisive victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-navas-de-tolosa">Las Navas de Tolosa</a> in 1212. That battle broke Almohad power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> and accelerated the decline of the Almohad Caliphate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfonso-viii.jpg" alt="Alfonso VIII" width="320" height="605" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alfons8_Tumbo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The caliphate's military power reached its zenith under Caliph Abu Yusuf Yaqub al-Mansur (r. 1184–1199), who won the empire's most celebrated victory at the Battle of Alarcos on 18 July 1195, where his forces crushed the Castilian army of <b>Alfonso VIII</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate · Military</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Alfonso VIII</b> took Cuenca in 1177 but was crushed by the Almohads at the Battle of Alarcos in 1195.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Kingdom of Castile · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Partition followed the murder of Sancho IV at Peñalén in 1076, and in 1200 Navarre lost Álava and Gipuzkoa, and with them its coast, to <b>Alfonso VIII of Castile</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-navarre">Kingdom of Navarre · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The Almohad caliph Abu Yusuf Yaqub al-Mansur defeated King <b>Alfonso VIII</b> of Castile, whose army retreated to Toledo, while the Almohads retook Trujillo, Montánchez and Talavera.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/july-18">18 July in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soria">Soria</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. Died in Gutierre-Muñoz, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=41.77,-2.47&amp;year=1193" aria-label="Soria on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4490 676 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Alfonso VIII"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4940 946h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4940 946h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=41.77,-2.47&amp;year=1193">What was here in 1193? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
